  {
   "phrase": 1,
   "start": 0.04,
   "end": 6.72,
   "text": "The war in Gaza was one of the most precise military operations in urban warfare history."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 2,
   "start": 6.72,
   "end": 11.61,
   "text": "Hamas attempted to massacre Jews in Israel, took hundreds of hostages,"
  },
  {
   "phrase": 3,
   "start": 11.61,
   "end": 18.03,
   "text": "murdered over a thousand people, and used civilian areas for military operations."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 4,
   "start": 18.03,
   "end": 28.7,
   "text": "If there really was a genocide, why did Gaza's population increase during the war? During a real genocide, there is a population decrease."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 5,
   "start": 28.74,
   "end": 33.29,
   "text": "Hamas fired thousands of rockets into Israel on a weekly basis."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 6,
   "start": 33.29,
   "end": 36.51,
   "text": "Now, there are zero rocket attacks."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 7,
   "start": 36.51,
   "end": 40.59,
   "text": "The moment they released the hostages, the war ended."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 8,
   "start": 40.59,
   "end": 51.27,
   "text": "Hamas attempted genocide against Israelis. Its founding charter explicitly calls for Israel's destruction and invokes the killing of Jews worldwide."
  },
  {
   "phrase": 9,
   "start": 51.27,
   "end": 52.99,
   "text": "That's classic Gazalighting."
  }
